[0.0, "o", "JSO\u001b[22;62H\u001b[38;5;130m    \u001b[39mN. Instead of asking for JSON in a text prompt (which c\u001b[23;62H\u001b[38;5;130m    \u001b[39man drift in for\u0007\u001b[1;40r\u001b[23;81H\u001b[?25l\u001b[?2026lmat), we define a tool whose input schem\u001b[24;62H\u001b[38;5;130m    \u001b[39ma matches \u001b[35m`\u001b[39mParsedReceipt\u001b[35m`\u001b[39m. Claude \"calls\" the tool with\u001b[25;62H\u001b[38;5;130m    \u001b[39m the extracted data, giving us guaranteed-valid JSON. T\u001b[26;62H\u001b[38;5;130m    \u001b[39mhis avoids the need for retry/validation loops.\u001b[27;62H\u001b[38;5;130m 43 \u001b[28;62H 44 \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[35m### Category assignment\u001b[29;62H\u001b[38;5;130m 45 \u001b[30;62H 46 \u001b[39mWe'll provide a fixed set of categories in the prompt (\u001b[31;62H\u001b[38;5;130m    \u001b[39mGroceries, Dining, Electronics, Health, Household, Clot\u001b[32;62H\u001b[38;5;130m    \u001b[39mhing, Transportation, Entertainment, Other). Claude ass\u001b[33;62H\u001b[38;5;130m    \u001b[39migns one per item. Keeping the list fixed now means we \u001b[34;62H\u001b[38;5;130m    \u001b[39mcan aggregate by category later without normalization h\u001b[35;62H\u001b[38;5;130m    \u001b[39meadaches.\u001b[36;62H\u001b[38;5;130m 47 \u001b[37;62H"]
